olvement)"], "excluded_candidates": ["Primary ciliary dyskinesia with respiratory and sinus manifestations: less likely to explain constitutional growth delay and airway dilation alone", "Connective tissue disorder with multisystem involvement: unexplained by isolated tricuspid stenosis and airway dilation alone", "Congenital diaphragmatic hernia or thoracic mass: inconsistent with MRI findings of airway dilation rather than mass effect"], "alarm_features": ["Chronic progressive multisystem involvement", "Growth delay since birth"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Cystic Fibrosis with Pulmonary and Systemic Features", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0, "posterior": 0.713143231511754, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Airway dilation on MRI is a classic finding in cystic fibrosis, providing moderate support for B1 as a potential diagnosis."], "evidence_against": ["Undone sweat chloride testing weakens the ability to confirm cystic fibrosis, resulting in a minor reduction of B1’s likelihood."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.9, "interrupt_relevance": 0.75, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "etiology", "representative_diseases": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Primary Ciliary Dyskinesia with Chronic Infections", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.248, "danger": 0.6, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Genetic Pulmonary Hypertension Syndrome", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.0, "danger": 0.9, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The lack of left ventricular dysfunction, antiphospholipid antibodies, or von Willebrand abnormalities provides strong evidence against genetic pulmonary hyper…"]}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "labe